{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtJLuqWuqey2QQSQVJb9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Summing attention over all earlier cycles reveals a clear induction circuit. Inside the loops, layer 15 head 7 puts 85% of its attention on \"the token that followed an earlier occurrence of the current context\". So do layer 23 head 5 (74%), layer 11 head 1 (71%), layer 19 head 5 (47%), and layer 23 heads 0/4/7 (~45%). That compares with 15–48% before the loop. There are also strong duplicate-token heads (layer 7 heads 5/6/7, layer 3 head 7, layer 23 head 6). Attention patterns alone don't prove these heads write the loop prediction. So next I'll do a direct-logit decomposition from the returned hidden states: how much each layer's mixer (attention/DeltaNet) and MLP output pushes up the logit of the actual next token, in loop versus pre-loop positions. First I'll check whether `hidden_24` is pre- or post-final-norm by comparing its logit-lens output against the returned top-k log-probs.\n\n```python\n# Hypothesis: (check) hidden_24 is post-final-norm; verify via logit lens against returned topk to set up DLA correctly.\nH = {l: np.load(D5 + f'hidden_{l}.npy', mmap_mode='r') for l in range(25)}\ntk_ids = np.load(D5 + 'topk_ids.npy'); tk_lp = np.load(D5 + 'topk_logprobs.npy'); tlp = np.load(D5 + 'token_logprobs.npy')\nEt = E  # embedding (tied unembedding), float32 torch\nwf = load_original('model.language_model.norm.weight')\nb, i = 0, 1500\nfor l in [23, 24]:\n    x = torch.tensor(np.asarray(H[l][b, i]))\n    print(l, 'rms', x.pow(2).mean().sqrt().item())\nx24 = torch.tensor(np.asarray(H[24][b, i])); x23 = torch.tensor(np.asarray(H[23][b, i]))\nlg_a = Et @ x24                                     # if post-norm\nlg_b = Et @ (x24 / x24.pow(2).mean().add(1e-6).sqrt() * (1 + wf))   # if pre-norm\nfor nm, lg in [('post', lg_a), ('pre', lg_b)]:\n    lp = torch.log_softmax(lg, 0)\n    print(nm, 'top ids', torch.topk(lp, 5).indices.tolist(), 'returned', tk_ids[b, i, :5].tolist(), 'lp', lp[tk_ids[b, i, 0]].item(), tk_lp[b, i, 0])\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1890,"cache_read_input_tokens":78556,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1890},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"37ae3ac5-393a-4da3-8caf-f8ba0ea8f929","uuid":"e1dca4a2-9a24-4554-9d60-82a546b35e18","timestamp":"2026-11-10T00:28:06.054Z","request_id":"req_011CgtJLuF3gjXYfiiF1Rz4W"}
